y-job-new-michigan-ad-hired","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel and Dan Wetzel","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Bottom 10 after Week 12: How the Bruins put the 'L' in UCLA","description":"While UCLA suffered its first loss, we still have a team looking for its first win -- and time is running out.","published":"2026-11-25T12:14:25.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50585901/bottom-10-week-12-ucla","type":"Story","byline":"Ryan McGee","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What went wrong for Michigan and Ohio State in 2026?","description":"Michigan and Ohio State have combined for nine losses entering Saturday's game.","published":"2026-11-25T12:25:19.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50576202/michigan-wolverines-ohio-state-buckeyes-went-wrong","type":"Story","byline":"Adam Rittenberg and Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Best bets for rivalry week: Breaking down Michigan-OSU, Iowa-Nebraska and more","description":"Pamela Maldonado and Mark Zinno break down the best bets they see around college football for rivalry week.","published":"2026-11-25T11:46:21.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50583508/college-football-betting-week-13-rivalry-week","type":"Story","byline":"Pamela Maldonado and Mark Zinno","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What are the conference title game clinching scenarios in Week 13?","description":"Plenty of spots are still up for grabs entering the final week of the regular season.","published":"2026-11-25T03:40:06.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50583399/conference-title-game-clinching-scenarios-week-13","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"College football betting: Should you still bet on Indiana to make the CFP?","description":"The Hoosiers dropped to No. 14 in the latest CPF rankings, but are they still a good bet to make the playoff?","published":"2026-11-25T04:16:33.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50588403/2026-college-football-playoff-cfp-indiana-hoosiers","type":"Story","byline":"Pamela Maldonado","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Week 12 Anger Index: Indiana dropped how many spots?!","description":"Ranking the teams that should be most upset with the latest CFP rankings.","published":"2026-11-25T14:21:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50582371/cfp-ranking-2026-anger-index-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"David Hale","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who's on the College Football Playoff bubble after committee's fourth ranking?","description":"A conference-by-conference look at which teams are contending for the playoff, who's close and who's out.","published":"2026-11-25T14:12:36.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575185/cfp-playoff-2026-bubble-watch-week-fourth-ranking","type":"Story","byline":"Heather Dinich","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5112674/bryant-wesco-jr","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bryant_Wesco"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Bryant Wesco","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bryant_Wesco","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-22T04:17:38Z","intro":"Bryant Wesco Jr. (born September 22, 2005) is an American college football wide receiver for the Clemson Tigers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Wesco was born on September 22, 2005, and grew up in Midlothian, Texas. He attended Midlothian High School, where he competed in football and track. After playing on the freshman football team in 2020, he made the varsity as a sophomore in 2021 and made 17 receptions for 212 yards and four touchdowns. As a junior in 2022, he recorded 56 receptions for 1,072 yards and 12 touchdowns, despite Midlothian using a run-heavy playbook. In his senior year, Wesco caught 36 passes for 619 yards and 13 touchdowns, despite appearing in just seven games. He concluded his high school career having totaled 109 catches for 1,903 yards and 29 touchdowns, averaging 17.5 yards-per-reception.\nWesco was invited to the Under Armour All-America Game and to the Polynesian Bowl. A five-star prospect, he was a consensus top 35 recruit in the nation and was ranked in the top 25 by PrepStar (15), 247Sports (22) and ESPN (25). He committed to play college football for the Clemson Tigers."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Wesco entered Clemson as an early enrollee in January 2024. He received his first start in the second game of the season and caught a 76-yard touchdown pass against Appalachian State."}]}}